+Which subset of the interrupts is considered fast interrupts is controlled by {fithresh}.
+The highest legal value of {mipreemptcfg}.{fithresh} is IPRIOLEN.
+
+NOTE: In the intended use-case, {fithresh} will be configured to values smaller than {preemptmsk}.
+This selects a subset of preemption groups as fast-interrupts.
+
+[source,subs="attributes"]
+----
+FITHRESHOLD = 2^mipreemptcfg.fithresh
+----
+
+An interrupt source is considered a fast interrupt source depending on its IPRIO value, if the following condition holds:
+
+[source]
+----
+IPRIO < FITHRESHOLD
+
+which is equivalent to
+
+IPRIO & FITHRESHOLD == 0
+----
+
+NOTE: The fast interrupt threshold is defined this way to simplify the logic to determine,
+if an interrupt is considered a fast interrupt.
+No comparator is needed this way, and the determination can be done through a bitwise and-operation.
